    "result_text": "All tests pass. \n\nThe change was confined to a single file, `AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n\n- Builds `customerCode` as `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where CITY3 and LAST3 are the upper-cased first three letters of city and lastName, and NNNN is a per-city sequence (count of existing owners in that city, plus one).\n- Extracted two tiny private helpers (`prefix3`, `countInCity`) so the `service` method stays simple rather than growing.\n\nThe membership number needed no edit: `MembershipNumber.of` just prefixes the customerCode (`%s-M%02d`), so it automatically rebuilds on the new format. The acceptance test verifying the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` shape and the full suite are green.",
